msgid "low_bell_alda_garden_thanks"
msgstr "Alda: It chose the upper pasture once it had room. Good—gardens should feed creatures, not trap them."

msgid "low_bell_alda_intro"
msgstr "Alda: Caper ate seedlings before. They never slept under my tool bench until that tone began."

msgid "low_bell_alda_resolved"
msgstr "Alda: No one under the bench this morning. I had forgotten how welcome an ordinary bite mark could look."

msgid "low_bell_archive_diagram"
msgstr "The diagram shows three tuned bells, each with a narrow metal tongue. A note in Mara's hand reads: LOW TONE IS NOT A WARNING SIGNAL."

msgid "low_bell_assembly_action"
msgstr "You close the survey cut and wedge the loose tongue clear of the fractured bell stone. Water returns to the old drain."

msgid "low_bell_bren_intro"
msgstr "Bren: These hairline cracks are old. The fresh grit inside them is not. I can tell you that much and no more."

msgid "low_bell_bren_resolved"
msgstr "Bren: Iven bought drain stone. I made him buy inspection markers too."

msgid "low_bell_campaign"
msgstr "Ashenbell: The Low Bell"

msgid "low_bell_caro_intro"
msgstr "Caro: Three guests heard a ghost; two heard weather; one slept through it. That is why I serve breakfast, not conclusions."

msgid "low_bell_caro_resolved"
msgstr "Caro: Tonight's wager is whether the inn can be quiet enough for anyone to complain."

msgid "low_bell_ending_hook"
msgstr "Nera pins a courier note beside the revised memorial notice: the western valley has reported the same displaced Corvix flight."

msgid "low_bell_garden_caper"
msgstr "A displaced Caper has nested between the seed rows. It stamps at every vibration from the north."

msgid "low_bell_hoist_apply"
msgstr "You divert the trickle, seat the cradle brace, then ease the hoist brake. The chamber floor settles instead of ringing."

msgid "low_bell_iven_intro"
msgstr "Iven: A working warning line would be useful. Abandonment has not made this village safer—or richer."

msgid "low_bell_iven_investigation"
msgstr "Iven: I paid for a survey, nothing more. If a cleared ditch frightens people, perhaps the ditch needed attention."

msgid "low_bell_iven_resolved"
msgstr "Iven: Ashenbell still needs work. Reopening blindly was not work; it was wishing with other people's risk."

msgid "low_bell_jemuar_after"
msgstr "Jemuar backs into a dry fissure. Without its weight, the note thins—but water still runs across the buried fitting."

msgid "low_bell_jemuar_reveal"
msgstr "A massive Jemuar rises beside the buried assembly. Each frightened step drives a lower note through stone and metal."

msgid "low_bell_jori_complete"
msgstr "Jori: Squabbit sleeps beside the warm wall now. If the stones hum, it comes to find me first."

msgid "low_bell_jori_intro"
msgstr "Jori: Squabbit follows noises under the floor. It ran north last night and did not come back."

msgid "low_bell_jori_resolved_complete"
msgstr "Jori: Squabbit did not chase the tone last night. We both heard ordinary rain, which is much better."

msgid "low_bell_jori_resolved_pending"
msgstr "Jori: The quarry path is safer now. I am going to keep watching for Squabbit's tracks."

msgid "low_bell_jori_return"
msgstr "Squabbit bounds from behind you. Jori laughs once, then grips its ears. 'No more following underground songs. These are for you.'"

msgid "low_bell_jori_searching"
msgstr "Jori: Squabbit likes dry ledges where a low noise tickles its feet. It hates running water, so look above the quarry runnel."

msgid "low_bell_kesh_after"
msgstr "Kesh: The old rubbing is beside the high marker. The wind cache beyond it was left for crews caught above cloud."

msgid "low_bell_kesh_challenge"
msgstr "Kesh: Corvix keep striking my survey flags. Help me test their pattern; if you hold your ground, I can finish the rubbing."

msgid "low_bell_kesh_victory"
msgstr "Kesh: They broke east on the same gust that carried the tone. Take the medicine—I have the observation I needed."

msgid "low_bell_lower_collapse"
msgstr "Broken shift boards remain where the roof fell. The final line is smeared, but the inspection boxes were never signed."

msgid "low_bell_mara_intro"
msgstr "Mara: It is not one of our warning bells. Say that clearly before a rumour says otherwise."

msgid "low_bell_mara_investigation"
msgstr "Mara: The old bells were measured, named and maintained. This tone is lower. Ask Sela what the ridge is carrying."

msgid "low_bell_mara_names_complete"
msgstr "Mara aligns the three records. 'Ina Vel. Oren Pike. Mett Saro. The memorial will not leave blank spaces where people stood.'"

msgid "low_bell_mara_names_offer"
msgstr "Mara: Three names on the silent-shift roll are weathered away. If you find marked tokens or rubbings, bring the facts—not guesses."

msgid "low_bell_mara_names_progress"
msgstr "Mara: The pass survey shelf and the old quarry pockets carried duplicate shift marks. Record only what you can read."

msgid "low_bell_mara_resolved"
msgstr "Mara: The silent memorial remains. This year we will also read the maintenance oath—the part everyone stopped reading."

msgid "low_bell_mara_resolved_names"
msgstr "Mara: The maintenance oath will be read beneath all the names—including the three you returned. Memory must include what the work demanded."

msgid "low_bell_name_pass_found"
msgstr "A charcoal rubbing preserves a second line: OREN PIKE, HOIST WATCH. The paper is recent; the carved mark is not."

msgid "low_bell_name_quarry_found"
msgstr "A brass strip reads METT SARO, CRADLE RIGGER. A sealed emergency wrap behind it still contains a Revive."

msgid "low_bell_name_south_found"
msgstr "A weathered shift token is wedged behind the overlook stone: INA VEL, DRAIN CREW. The ridge line matches Mara's memorial map."

msgid "low_bell_nera_after_tutorial"
msgstr "Nera: Good. You gave it room to retreat. Take these Tuxeballs—some displaced creatures may accept a calmer approach."

msgid "low_bell_nera_clear_path"
msgstr "Nera: The frightened Shybulb ahead cannot settle while we crowd it. Approach slowly; I will talk you through the battle."

msgid "low_bell_nera_investigation"
msgstr "Nera: Creatures are leaving wet ground from here to the South Approach. We need the source, not a story about it."

msgid "low_bell_nera_opening"
msgstr "Nera: That was no thunder. Stay close—those creatures are running from something."

msgid "low_bell_nera_resolved"
msgstr "Nera: Habitat is a better witness than rumour. The creatures are already drawing the new map for us."

msgid "low_bell_nera_starter"
msgstr "Nera: You need a partner, not a weapon. Choose the one whose way of working makes sense to you."

msgid "low_bell_nera_town"
msgstr "Nera: Garden species moved first, then woodland species. Whatever changed is travelling downhill through water or ground."

msgid "low_bell_opening_tone"
msgstr "A low note rolls under the rain. Leaves jump; frightened creatures spill onto the path."

msgid "low_bell_pell_intro"
msgstr "Pell: The north post is closed, so every courier is sharing the South Approach. Find the cause and you will reopen more than a road."

msgid "low_bell_pell_resolved"
msgstr "Pell: The north post wants a field report from the western valley. Nera already put your name beside mine."

msgid "low_bell_puzzle_cradle"
msgstr "You seat the CRADLE brace into the unloaded frame. The resonant slab stops shifting."

msgid "low_bell_puzzle_hoist"
msgstr "You ease the HOIST brake last. The frame settles, and its service cage opens a route back to the pass."

msgid "low_bell_puzzle_runoff"
msgstr "You turn the labelled RUNOFF gate. Water leaves the fractured shelf and enters the old drain."

msgid "low_bell_puzzle_wrong"
msgstr "The control will not move safely in this state. The three labels repeat the maintenance order: RUNOFF — CRADLE — HOIST."

msgid "low_bell_quarry_fitting"
msgstr "A bent metal tongue lies pinned under resonant stone. Rust is old; bright scrapes around the drainage bolt are recent."

msgid "low_bell_quarry_fork"
msgstr "Fresh cart ruts cut across the abandoned track. Blue survey cloth is caught on a stone pointing east."

msgid "low_bell_ren_after"
msgstr "Ren: The grass here gives creatures an exit. Weaken one, then offer a Tuxeball—do not corner it."

msgid "low_bell_ren_challenge"
msgstr "Ren: I am carrying medicine uphill, but the wet pocket is full of skittish creatures. A short match will show whether your partner is ready to help."

msgid "low_bell_ren_victory"
msgstr "Ren: Steady enough. Take this potion; a courier who arrives empty-handed has only delivered a problem."

msgid "low_bell_return_for_tovin"
msgstr "The fresh survey marks match Tovin's hoist sketch. His workshop may hold the safe way into the lower works."

msgid "low_bell_return_iven"
msgstr "Iven: My crew opened the western runnel. I hid that because I wanted the survey to look harmless. I will pay to make it safe."

msgid "low_bell_return_mara"
msgstr "Mara: We will keep the names and retire the machinery. A memorial is not an instruction to repeat the past."

msgid "low_bell_return_nera"
msgstr "Nera: Shybulb are back at the stream, and the garden Squabbit stopped digging at the foundations. The pressure is easing."

msgid "low_bell_return_objective"
msgstr "The chamber falls quiet. Return to Ashenbell; the village needs the whole account."

msgid "low_bell_return_tovin"
msgstr "Tovin: I approved that last shift. Silence did not change it. I can still teach the next crew where to stop."

msgid "low_bell_rockat_after"
msgstr "The Rockat retreats to a dry shelf. The lower gate is clear, and its old brace marks match Tovin's sequence."

msgid "low_bell_rockat_guard"
msgstr "A Rockat claws at the lower gate whenever the runoff touches stone. It is cornered between the tone and the open track."

msgid "low_bell_rook_after"
msgstr "Rook: Corvix have left the west face. Rockitten are climbing out of cracks they normally sleep in. That is a direction, not bad luck."

msgid "low_bell_rook_challenge"
msgstr "Rook: The upper pass has nowhere to hide from wind or a panicked monster. Show me you can hold a line without chasing."

msgid "low_bell_rook_victory"
msgstr "Rook: Good footing. Split Crown is loudest on the east shelf; follow the rock, not the echo."

msgid "low_bell_secret_pass"
msgstr "The wind cache contains two Earth Tuxeballs, wrapped against grit and rain."

msgid "low_bell_secret_south"
msgstr "Under the stream marker, a courier's waxed pouch still holds a Super Potion."

msgid "low_bell_sela_enter"
msgstr "Sela: That matches the old maintenance marks. I will watch the runnel; use Tovin's order in the lower works."

msgid "low_bell_sela_investigation"
msgstr "Sela: Every report follows heavy runoff and a west wind. Split Crown carries the tone; the source lies beyond its east shoulder."

msgid "low_bell_sela_need_tovin"
msgstr "Sela: I can prove where the water went. Tovin is the one who knows what is carrying the load below it. Bring me his sequence."

msgid "low_bell_settlement_reveal"
msgstr "Ashenbell appears beyond the trees. Far above its roofs, Split Crown Ridge divides the cloud."

msgid "low_bell_south_rail"
msgstr "The old guide rail hums against the stream stones. Tiny tracks point uphill, away from the wet bank."

msgid "low_bell_split_crown_tone"
msgstr "The low tone arrives through the ridge before it reaches the air. Loose stones chatter toward the quarry fork."

msgid "low_bell_squabbit_found"
msgstr "A mud-streaked Squabbit crouches on the dry ledge. At Jori's name it chirps, then follows at a careful distance."

msgid "low_bell_survey_disturbance"
msgstr "The survey stake bears Iven's trade mark. A freshly cleared runnel sends rainwater beneath a slab labelled LOWER RESONANCE BAY."

msgid "low_bell_tovin_briefing"
msgstr "Tovin studies the survey mark. 'That runnel fed the lower fracture. Brace the cradle before you touch the hoist, or the stone will answer.'"

msgid "low_bell_tovin_initial"
msgstr "Tovin: Hoists, drains, bells—people remember the nouns and forget the inspection. I will not help anyone reopen that place."

msgid "low_bell_tovin_reminder"
msgstr "Tovin: Water first. Brace second. Hoist last. The order kept weight off the cracked shelf."

msgid "low_bell_tovin_resolved"
msgstr "Tovin: I kept the procedure and buried the reason. Mara was right: facts cannot protect anyone if we refuse to speak them."

msgid "low_bell_tovin_resolved_names"
msgstr "Tovin: Mett Saro set that cradle beside me. Seeing his name restored does not excuse my signature. It tells me who my silence excluded."

msgid "low_bell_tutorial_creature"
msgstr "The Shybulb shivers, then plants itself across the path."

msgid "low_bell_village_arrival"
msgstr "The memorial square is busy, but nobody is celebrating."
